  "notes": "Surface is one grammar alternative ('*' in <highlight-name-selector>) plus the two cascade consequences the spec and WPT define for it (zero specificity / per-property merge; inheritance through the originating element tree). The parent ::highlight(<custom-ident>) and the HighlightRegistry/Highlight APIs are pre-existing surface (Chrome 105, MDN-covered) and are referenced, not re-inventoried. Positive-path behaviour could not be executed locally: the sandbox has Chrome 153, and the CSSCustomHighlightUniversalSelector runtime flag is absent there (enabling it had no effect); only the pre-158 rejection path (insertRule SyntaxError, CSS.supports false, \\* parses) was observed. Positive behaviour is documented from the spec text and WPT assertions, with wpt.fyi pass status cited. getComputedStyle(el, '::highlight(*)') is deliberately left undocumented beyond 'not covered by WPT'."
